{"title":"1985 AJHSME Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a certain year, January had exactly four Tuesdays and four Saturdays.  On what day did January <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fall that year?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855472c4977479481560a88152286eb794fb7d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\text{Monday} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\text{Tuesday} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\text{Wednesday} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\text{Friday} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\text{Saturday}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"596\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>January has 31 days. If January 1 was on Monday or Tuesday, then there would have been 5 Tuesdays in the month. Similarly, if January 1 was on a Friday or Saturday, then there would have been 5 Saturdays in the month. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c30566eb8cdc9bedece6cf3fe5e9f72d50b979e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(C)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />  yjthis is not the case thign here is that if you would g for the world\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report